## 3. Architecture Layers

The app follows the standard Clean Architecture flow:

```
UI (Compose) -> ViewModel -> Use Case -> Repository -> Data Source
```

### 3.1 Presentation Layer

Each feature module exposes Compose screens backed by a `ViewModel` that exposes a `StateFlow<UiState>` (sealed class hierarchy: `Loading` / `Success` / `Error`) and consumes events via a sealed `Event` class. ViewModels are registered with Koin (`@KoinViewModel` or `viewModel { }`) and are screen-scoped.

### 3.2 Domain Layer

`prayer:domain` contains the repository interfaces (`IPrayerRepository`), the calculation service interface (`PrayerCalculationService`), the calculation engine (`PrayerTimeEngine`, `PrayerLogicEngine`), and use cases grouped by area (`prayer`, `location`, `quran`, `qibla`). `prayer:model` holds the shared data classes (`Prayer`, `DailyPrayer`, `CalculationMethod`, `JuristicMethod`, `LocationData`, `City`, `QiblaState`, etc.).

### 3.3 Data Layer

`prayer:data` implements the repository interfaces and data sources. Persistence is DataStore-based (see section 4). Remote access lives in `prayer_remote` (see section 8).

