## 5. Prayer Time Calculation — adhan2

`PrayerTimeEngine` (`prayer:domain`) implements `PrayerCalculationService` using the adhan2 library. It maps the app's `CalculationMethod` / `JuristicMethod` to adhan2 parameters and returns the six daily prayers, converting times into the prayer's time zone.

Real snippet — `PrayerTimeEngine`:

```kotlin
@Factory
class PrayerTimeEngine : PrayerCalculationService {
    override fun calculateDailyPrayerTimes(
        latitude: Double,
        longitude: Double,
        zoneId: ZoneId,
        date: LocalDateTime,
        calculationMethod: CalculationMethod,
        juristicMethod: JuristicMethod
    ): List<Prayer> {
        val coordinates = Coordinates(latitude, longitude)
        val dateComponents = DateComponents.fromLocalDateTime(date)
        val params = getCalculationParameters(calculationMethod, juristicMethod)
        val prayerTimes = PrayerTimes(coordinates, dateComponents, params)
        val kotlinTimeZone = zoneId.toKotlinTimeZone()
        return listOf(
            Prayer("Fajr", "الفجر", prayerTimes.fajr.toLocalDateTime(kotlinTimeZone).time, date.date),
            Prayer("Sunrise", "الشروق", prayerTimes.sunrise.toLocalDateTime(kotlinTimeZone).time, date.date),
            Prayer("Dhuhr", "الظهر", prayerTimes.dhuhr.toLocalDateTime(kotlinTimeZone).time, date.date),
            Prayer("Asr", "العصر", prayerTimes.asr.toLocalDateTime(kotlinTimeZone).time, date.date),
            Prayer("Maghrib", "المغرب", prayerTimes.maghrib.toLocalDateTime(kotlinTimeZone).time, date.date),
            Prayer("Isha", "العشاء", prayerTimes.isha.toLocalDateTime(kotlinTimeZone).time, date.date)
        )
    }
}
```

Supported calculation methods: Turkey Diyanet, MWL, ISNA, Egypt, Makkah, Karachi; madhab SHAFI / HANAFI. `PrayerLogicEngine` handles countdown and current/next prayer selection using an injectable `Clock` for deterministic tests.

